    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0337" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg241"/>

                <head>No. 117.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Wing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-10-13"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 13,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th instant and its accompaniments in regard to the refusal
                    of the collector of internal revenue at San Francisco to accept as bondsmen for
                    tobacco manufacturers wealthy Chinese merchants. In reply, I beg leave to inform
                    you that the subject has been submitted to the Secretary of the Treasury, who
                    has competent jurisdiction over, affairs of that character.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, renewed assurance of my very high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
